artifacts/*
# reproducers are the actual G6 deliverable (small markdown, filed
# upstream by hand) - unlike the multi-GB sweep/corpus artifacts they
# need to be committed, not regenerated. git can't re-include a path
# whose parent dir is excluded by a trailing-slash pattern, hence
# artifacts/* (per-entry) above instead of artifacts/ (whole subtree).
!artifacts/reproducers/
# result_hash.txt is a single small hex digest (G7's deliverable), not
# a regenerable multi-GB artifact - same reasoning as reproducers above.
!artifacts/result_hash.txt
.venv/
target/
__pycache__/
# internal process docs (design rationale, binding rules, append-only
# work log) - kept on disk for local development, never published.
DESIGN-FINAL.md
CLAUDE.md
START-HERE.md
WORKLOG.md
*.egg-info/
*.pyc
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
